{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-110969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 0=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get the false statement $0=12.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(C).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110969" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-110969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110969" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74198" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-74198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74198" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $M$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{m}_{1}+{x}_{2}{m}_{2},$ and ${m}_{1},$  ${m}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $M.$ \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ we need to check if the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}=8 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=6.$  \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Mx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(M).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${m}_{1}$ and ${m}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=6\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{m}_{2}}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=6(-2)=-12.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-110955" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110955" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Col}(M)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110955" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $F$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{f}_{1}+{x}_{2}{f}_{2},$ and ${f}_{1},$  ${f}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $F.$\n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(F),$ we need to check if the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[F\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[F\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -14\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives  ${x}_{1}=1.$ \n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Fx=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(F).$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${f}_{1}$ and ${f}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=1\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{1}}+(-2)\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{f}_{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=1\\cdot (-2)=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34366" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-34366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Col}(F)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34366" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & \\,\\,-1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\,-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ \\,\\,-2 & \\,\\,-2 & 2 \\\\ \\,\\,-1 & \\,\\,-1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,\\,-4 \\\\ 0 & \\,\\,2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=-6 \\\\ 0=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get the false statement $0=1.$ \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110938" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-110938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110938" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ k \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=k \\\\ 0=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110979" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-110979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-21"] ["math" "-23"] ["math" "-31"] ["math" "-32"] ["math" "40"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110979" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-21"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix given by $B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k-3\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(B).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(B),$ then the equation $Bx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[B\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[B\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 7 & k-3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k+2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=k-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k-1,$ which means that $k=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74209" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-74209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74209" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-35562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-35562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -7 & 7 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 17 & k-12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-17){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=k+5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=k+5,$ which means that $k=-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-35562" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-35562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-35562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-35562" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix given by $L=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}7k-1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(L).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(L),$ then the equation $Lx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[L\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[L\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -1 & 7k-1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 8 & -1 & 7k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=(-\\frac{1}{4}){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -9 & 7k-25\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7k-7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2 \\\\ 0=7k-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=7k-7,$ which means that $k=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110976" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-110976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-110976" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrix given by $M=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2k+10\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(M).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(M),$ then the equation $Mx=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[M\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[M\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 15 & 2k+10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2k-10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}=4 \\\\ 0=2k-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=2k-10,$ which means that $k=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-74213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "20"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-74213" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix $D$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(D).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}$, where ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$, ${x}_{3}$, and ${x}_{4}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{d}_{1}+{x}_{2}{d}_{2}+{x}_{3}{d}_{3}+{x}_{4}{d}_{4},$ and ${d}_{1}$, ${d}_{2}$, ${d}_{3}$, and ${d}_{4}$ are respective columns of $D.$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(D),$ we need to check if the equation $Dx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[D\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[D\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 4 & 7 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 & -1 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}+7{x}_{4}=11 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=-2 \\\\ 0=9 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}-{x}_{4}=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get a false statement $0=9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(D).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb1a6717ab693ec0afe7d43e2ce0cf3f4b1decbbda17833059c0d0a4db4e4d61"} {"question" "q-34346" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14064257/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d96c38612cdde1be4c847596728e163a1b542ae0ab3274c80438acf68df03b68"} {"question" "q-34346" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/referenc